> Included Software

SNAPS-OS comes with a small inclusion of software on top of your base install (which can be any kind of arch-based OS)

#from the Arch User Repository (AUR):

(aur)mangowm-git - the git version of mangoWM, you *can* choose to swap this out for a pacman repository version if you wish
(aur)dsearch-bin - indexer for file search from Dank Material Shell
(aur)qt6ct-kde - QT6 configuration tool for KDE-style QT theming
(aur)adwsteamgtk - applies adw-gtk theme colors to Steam
(aur)dcal - the Dank Calendar daemon for DMS

#from the pacman repositories:

[^apps]:
firefox - included browser
nautilus - included file browser
satty - included screenshot annotation editor
dms-shell - Dank Material Shell environment
shelly - default package management GUI interface
code (vscode-oss) - default GUI code editor, used for opening project directories
yazi - terminal file manager with image previews
cava - terminal audio visualizer
btop - interactive system resource monitor and process manager

[^terminal]:
ghostty - included pre-configured GPU-accelerated terminal
zsh - included shell
zsh-theme-powerlevel10k - theming for zsh
zsh-history-substring-search - plugin for zsh
zsh-syntax-highlighting - plugin for zsh
zsh-autosuggestions - plugin for zsh
zsh-doc - documentation for zsh
stow - symlink management utility
zoxide - replaces CD with a smarter CD that can jump, making navigation easier
eza - replaces the ls command with a smarter ls using coloration, icons and extra info
fzf - used for TUIs, also integrated into the terminal with `**<tab>` for fzf search for arguments
micro - terminal text editor with mouse support and familiar keybinds
wtype - wayland-native keyboard input simulator, used by scripts

[^utilities]:
brightnessctl - allows screen brightness control
pipewire-pulse - audio server and routing
pipewire - display/audio capture framework
matugen - Material You color scheme generator for auto-theming
yay - AUR helper for installing packages from the AUR
wl-clipboard - wayland clipboard utilities used by scripts
hyprshot - screenshot tool for wayland (used by region captures)
grim - screenshot utility for wayland
jp2a - converts images to ASCII art (used in terminal)
tela-circle-icon-theme-black - icon theme for SNAPS-OS desktop
adw-gtk-theme - libadwaita GTK theme for auto-theming
python-gobject - Python bindings for GTK/GObject (needed for some DMS functionality)
python-cairo - Python bindings for Cairo graphics

[^fonts]:
ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols-common
ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols-mono
ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols
ttf-cascadia-code-nerd
ttf-cascadia-mono-nerd
ttf-terminus-nerd
ttf-firacode-nerd
ttf-ubuntu-nerd

[^optional extras]:
unipkg - cross-distro package manager wrapper TUI (super+shift+Y)
dotfile-git-sync - utility to manage and sync dotfiles to a GitHub repository
Distro Wallpapers - additional wallpaper collections for DMS
